      "last_edit_date": 0,
      "message_parsed": "<b>Notice</b>: crypt(): No salt parameter was specified. You must use a randomly generated salt and a strong hash function to produce a secure hash. in <b>common.php</b> on line <b>1991</b><br />\n<br />\n<code style=\"font-family: Monaco, 'Andale Mono', 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\nfont-size: 0.9em;\nfont-style: normal;\nline-height: 1.3em;\nbackground: #BFE6FF;\nborder: 1px solid #C6C6EA;\nborder-radius: 3.5px;\npadding: 1px 3px;\ncolor: #0F4D79;\ndisplay: inline-block;\nmargin-bottom: 2px;\">$str .= str_shuffle(preg_replace(&#039;#[^0-9a-zA-Z]#&#039;, &#039;&#039;, crypt(uniqid(mt_rand(), true))));<br />\n</code><br />\nзаменить на <br />\n<code style=\"font-family: Monaco, 'Andale Mono', 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\nfont-size: 0.9em;\nfont-style: normal;\nline-height: 1.3em;\nbackground: #BFE6FF;\nborder: 1px solid #C6C6EA;\nborder-radius: 3.5px;\npadding: 1px 3px;\ncolor: #0F4D79;\ndisplay: inline-block;\nmargin-bottom: 2px;\">$str .= str_shuffle(preg_replace(&#039;#[^0-9a-zA-Z]#&#039;, &#039;&#039;, crypt(&quot;uniqid(&#039;&#039;, true): %s\\r\\n&quot;, uniqid(&#039;&#039;, true))));</code>",
